#X text 660 20 bridge_slicer: REPLACES js_slicer_stub. Inlet 0 takes the EXACT SAME messages the original Max js object took (buildIndex \, start \, stop \, next <track> \, forceNext <stem|all> \, loop <track> <bars> \, unloop <track> \, lockSource <leader> <followers...> \, setSegmentBars \, setGlobalBPM \, etc -- see slicer_bridge.js's DISPATCH table for the full ~54-command list) -- unchanged from upstream's wiring \, since Pd's message-selector-first-in-list convention is identical to Max's. [pd packOSC] treats the message's own selector as the OSC address and the rest of the list as the OSC args -- same proven pattern as bridge_sliceWriter.pd., f 380;
#X text 660 250 4 outlets \, matching the original js object's outlet contract exactly: outlet 0 = playback trigger (track slot startFrac endFrac stretchRatio segDurMs cycleId groupSize -- plus tagged commands "resume"/"stop"/"preload"/"rescheduleLive"/"resumeSeek" \, all sharing this outlet like the original) \, outlet 1 = status/metadata (desc \, seg \, ready \, slices \, sysMsg \, ~80 different tags -- see slicer.js's original header comment for the full list) \, outlet 2 = descriptor dump (from dumpDescriptors) \, outlet 3 = query result count (from selectRange). Each arrives here as a plain Pd list with the original tag word first (e.g. "vocals 0 0.32 0.58 1.0 12000 3 4" on outlet 0 \, "desc vocals 1000 0.5 ..." on outlet 1) -- wire each outlet's downstream `route`/`select` objects exactly as the old js object's outlets were wired., f 380;
#X text 660 480 Start the bridge alongside Pd: node bridge/slicer_bridge.js --data-dir /path/to/EBYS/data --recv-port 9004 --send-port 9005 (ports must match the netsend "connect" message and the netreceive port above -- distinct from bridge_sliceWriter's 9002/9003 and bridge_streamWatcher's 9001 so all three can run at once).;
